WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.490
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.490
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.500
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.500
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.820
It’s finally here!

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.540
The next term is coming.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.810
It doesn’t matter if you hate it,
if you laugh, cry, or whatever:

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.560
it’s coming no matter what!

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.710
Eh? You’re not kidding!

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.000
But it’s okay, you still have time.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.910
You just need to start preparing now,
if you haven’t already.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.840
So, let’s work hard!

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.520
Class dismissed.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.350
Semester exams…

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.000
Semester exams…

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.170
I’m screwed, there are only ten days left!

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.560
Don’t make up problems that don’t exist.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.990
Momoi-sensei said that
we still have time, right?

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.370
You’re really observant, aren’t you?

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.200
Goodbye, Nozomu-kun! Kosaka-kun too!

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.390
I’m just an afterthought!

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.150
You two seem to be in a hurry.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.450
Papa’s trial #23.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.440
Devote ourselves to studying for a test!

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.170
Right?

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:35.240
Bye-bye.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.170
Nozomu-chan!

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.860
Bye-bye!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.470
See you tomorrow!

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.800
Kosaka-kun as well!

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.960
Okay! See you tomorrow!

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.850
I’m definitely just an afterthought!

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.100
Sheesh, you really do have good luck!

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.000
You’re close to the Ichijou sisters…

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.720
Also, you were treated well by the other twins at the Chigusa Veterinary Hospital.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.120
I don’t think I was treated particularly well…

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:08.360
Damn it! If I had had a goat that swallowed a piece of paper at my house…

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:12.730
Also, Ruru-chan and Rara-chan treat you very well…

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:16.470
I feel that wherever you go, there’ll always be a set of twins!

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.280
You will definitely be punished!

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.800
What are you talking about?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.870
Watch out!

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.220
Watch out!

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.450
No way!

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.630
Hey, hang in there, Nozomu.
Are you okay?

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.710
Even the balls were twins…

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.140
Am I being punished?

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.450
Ah, you’re awake.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.330
Momoi-sensei…

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.390
Ah, don’t force yourself.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.670
You just had a concussion.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.490
So Momoi-sensei is the nurse as well as the home economics teacher?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.500
You’re injured.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.880
Umm… Sensei, it must be hard for you.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:19.300
It must be very difficult to double as the home economics teacher and the doctor here.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.570
Eh? Home economics?

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.260
Ah, I see. So you’re the transfer student.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.760
I guess so…

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.980
You’re the one living at Sourin temple, next to the shrine of those twins, correct?

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:34.560
Umm… Sensei, what are you talking about?

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.040
Futami-kun! Futami-kun! Are you okay?

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.550
EH?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.160
You surprised me there, Futami-kun!

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.640
What’s with the two Momoi-senseis?

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.230
Damn it! If I had been hit by a ball…

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.370
Are you two twins?

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.820
Oh my, you didn’t know?

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:02.110
I’m the older one, Mai.
This is my younger sister, Ai.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.680
Is that so?

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.530
Another set of twins?

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:11.930
Even Sensei has a twin. I’m definitely surrounded by twins…

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.360
Onii-chan, welcome back!

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:17.480
Let’s go to the shrine of the twins together!

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.090
Come with us!

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.900
The shrine of the twins, huh?

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.590
Ah… welcome back, Nozomu-kun.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.360
I’m back.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.070
Let’s go, let’s go!

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:26.600
Okay.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:33.370
Every month, we purify it like this.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.190
Purify?

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:38.020
We do this so the twins’ spirits can rest in peace.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:38.020
Note: Miyabi literally says “to become a Buddha”,
i.e., to seek peace/release in Buddhist terminology.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.710
Spirits? Then the legend…

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:45.130
That’s right. The one where the twin sisters loved the same young man,

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:49.550
and because he couldn’t decide on his feelings, they both suffered.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:50.760
We know!

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.220
They really suffered
and became little birds.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.460
Then they flew up into the sky.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.980
Is it true?

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:03.530
Because of this grave, there are a lot of twins in this town.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:09.470
Nozomu-kun, do you know about the evil curse of the grave?

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.390
Evil curse?

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.910
If a pair of twins in this town likes the same person and suffers because of that,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:22.630
something terrible will happen.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.820
Something terrible?

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.390
Don’t worry, Nozomu-kun.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:33.600
There are lots of cute twins and all of them may seem very pretty.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.280
For now…

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.450
You really took that seriously!

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.430
Romantic legends like this exist all over Japan.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.430
For example,

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:52.030
the “Resistance Against the Emperor’s Virtue”, or “Maiden of Unai”, from the Manyoshu.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:52.030
Note: The Manyoshu is the oldest anthology of Japanese poetry, compiled in c. AD 770.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:57.430
All of them involve two girls liking the same person, then suffering, and then dying.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.960
They are legends of that type.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.790
It seems the maidens’ grave is a remnant of that.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.880
And so, this grave of the twins is…

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.200
It belongs to one of the legends.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:09.760
I see.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.410
So, what do you think, Nozomu-kun?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.910
What would you do if you were loved by a set of twins?

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:21.790
There’s no problem! We’re going to be Onii-chan’s brides together!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:25.790
That’s right! Rara will be the bride,
Ruru will be the wife!

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.240
Is that so? Thank you.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:33.030
You two, there’s still
a lot of time before that.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.870
You need to think carefully!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.750
In reality, that’s just not possible.
You have to choose one.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.080
Yes.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:45.210
If those twins who loved the man had thought it out carefully,

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:50.770
maybe they wouldn’t have needed to turn into little birds in order to live.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.290
“You have to choose one”, huh?

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:06.860
Come to think of it, none of them have actually thought about me romantically.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.450
Never mind that,
if I don’t start studying…

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:14.050
Eh? Stop it!

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:19.040
Quit it! It’s going to rip!

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:29.940
I guess I’ll have to borrow someone else’s notes.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.950
I don’t think it’s possible to borrow it from him…

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.690
Okay. Notes for English, right?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.440
Yeah. Please.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.660
Just wait a moment.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:54.100
Oh my, it’s Nozomu-chan! How nostalgic!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.620
Hello! It’s been a while.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:01.120
You’ve really grown. Come in, come in!

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.160
I’m just here today to get some notes.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.130
It’s okay, you don’t have to be that polite. Come!

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.190
I guess, but…

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.180
Sorry about that, but Mom still tends to be pushy.

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.520
Oh, that’s okay.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.000
Where’s Kaoruko-chan?

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.110
She’s shopping in front of the train station.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.790
She said, “I can’t study for the exam without a pink marker.”

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:29.000
Kaoruko-chan has always been like that.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.610
I would say so.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:31.570
Here you go.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.630
Ah, thank you. This really saves me.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:36.410
You’re welcome.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.890
This bedroom brings back memories.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.810
Astronomy books? You two also like constellations?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.750
Yeah, all because of you.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:51.360
Eh?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.170
Don’t you remember
when we were younger,

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.360
you talked about the stars with us all the time?

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:01.520
Ah, that’s Orion over there!

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.450
The three stars that are
lined up are so cute!

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.630
It’s like the three stars are friends, just like us!

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:13.570
Your eyes would always light up
whenever you talked about stars.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:16.340
Oh, it’s something that Dad taught me.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.850
When you changed schools, we felt… lonely.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:26.450
Therefore, Kaoruko asked Mom and Dad to buy us books about astronomy.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:27.350
Kaoruko-chan said so?

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.850
Yeah, and then…

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:35.380
Nozomu-chan is looking at the stars at this moment, right?

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.590
Yeah! Most definitely!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.260
He should be able to see the same stars over in Tokyo!

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:42.100
Yeah! He can definitely see them!

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:45.930
Let’s look at the same stars
as Nozomu-chan!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.540
Even when we’re separated,
we can see the same stars!

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:53.250
I see. So you two tried to look at the same stars as me, huh?

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.870
Let’s go somewhere we haven’t been in a while.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.140
Eh? Go where?

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.760
It feels good on the roof.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.260
LOOK THE OTHER WAY!

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:18.530
Yes, ma’am!

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.030
It’s okay now, Nozomu-chan!

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:28.820
Sumireko-chan? Hey, Sumireko-chan, wait for me!

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:38.780
Looks like the spring showers have passed.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:39.870
Yeah.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:43.210
Ah, it feels good.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.840
Hey, Nozomu-chan.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:12:00.900
Do you remember the incident on the ferris wheel in Fukubuku Park?

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.620
Eh? The ferris wheel… that time…

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:09.560
I want to be your bride when I grow up!

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:14.040
Me too! I want to be your bride too!

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.820
Eh? Really?

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:18.910
But… what should I do?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.090
There’s only one of me!

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:25.090
That’s okay! We’ll both
become your brides!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.350
Of course! We’ll be together with you as your wives!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.800
That day, we both proposed to you.

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.890
Why did Sumireko-chan bring this up all of a sudden?

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:40.960
Back then,

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:45.180
I was secretly envious of you and Kaoruko.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:45.620
Eh?

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:52.780
You were so lively, and Kaoruko was a lot more active than I was…

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:59.070
Even though we were playing together,
I was always left behind.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.940
I was always trying to catch up.

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.280
Is that so?

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.050
I felt the same way at the ferris wheel.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:11.560
Kaoruko proposed to you,
and I said I would as well.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.250
What does she mean?

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:17.430
Does that mean Sumireko-chan liked me back then?

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.710
I always thought that if the three of us were together, everything would be okay.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:23.970
The three of us, together?

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.190
Like the three stars that are together in Orion – always together.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:30.100
You, me, and Kaoruko.

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:35.040
Therefore, at that time, I couldn’t not propose as well.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.500
Is that so?

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:41.280
At that time, I was very envious of Kaoruko.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:42.470
Even now…

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:49.040
Even now, I’m often envious of her.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.920
She can say things that I can’t say and do things that I can’t do.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:59.480
We’re twins, but why can’t I be as good as her?

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:05.110
But, umm… Sumireko-chan,
you have your strong points as well.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.180
It was only you, Nozomu-chan.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.770
The only one who could distinguish between the two of us…

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.960
…was you.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:32.430
I never expected Sumireko-chan to think this way.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:37.390
Actually, this is the first time that I’ve talked with Sumireko-chan, alone.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.860
Ah, it’s the Laughing Boy! Incredible!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.690
He’s come up with a
new subject. Wonderful!

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:54.610
Kaoruko-chan?

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.140
So Billy did something bad.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.650
It was surprising!

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:04.070
But it’s very cute! He likes you, so he’s just trying to get your attention.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.130
No, it’s definitely NOT that.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:09.910
We often came here to play.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.290
You, Sumireko, and I.

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:18.830
We played hide and seek, house, tag…
It’s so nostalgic!

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.810
Really, it hasn’t changed much.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:28.390
I was told how you two watched the stars together.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.350
That you asked your parents to buy you books about the stars.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:38.520
Somehow, I feel happy that we were looking at the same stars…

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.040
It was because of Sumireko.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:44.960
I was the one who asked them, but Sumireko thought up the idea.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:49.240
Kaoruko-chan!
I’ve thought of a good idea!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.200
Nozomu-chan must be
really lonely in Tokyo.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.540
I’ve thought of a way to get rid of the loneliness.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:57.590
So, Sumireko-chan did…

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:04.210
Because I’m the elder of us…

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:07.590
everyone thinks I should be
the stronger one.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.640
That isn’t really the case, though.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:12.860
Sumireko is the one that can really think things through

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.600
and make decisions, and she really tries.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.250
Now that you mention it…

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:24.240
Nozomu-chan… I’ll lure the dog away. You’ll get the ball back.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:31.340
Umm… our ball fell into your yard.
Could you help us get it back?

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.050
Oh my, wait just a minute.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.830
Sumireko-chan is a bit more introverted,

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:39.170
but she tries very hard when it comes to facing whatever happens.

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:39.680
Is that so?

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:45.920
You remember the proposal at the ferris wheel in Fukubuku Park, right?

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.440
Eh? Yeah.

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:51.680
At the time, I guess I was in a rush.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:53.930
Rush?

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:58.660
The way that Sumireko does things

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:02.160
makes me think I don’t try hard enough as an older sister.

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:08.040
Therefore, I have to act more like an adult – so I proposed to you.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:13.300
If I didn’t say it before Sumireko,
I would seem like a kid.

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:17.620
I see now… that was what happened back then.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:19.300
You’re still thinking about it?

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.940
I’m not trying as hard as I should be.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:26.190
That’s okay. You’re also trying very hard as well.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:27.920
You’re not pulling my leg, are you?

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.210
No, not on this one.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.070
Let’s go!

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:37.010
Ah, sliding on grass!

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.260
We used to do it a lot.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.700
Wait up, you guys!

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:42.110
Kaoruko-chan!

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.540
Will you be okay, Miss?

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.050
Who do you think I am?

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.050
Kaoruko-chan.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:58.600
On your mark, get set, go!

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.460
Out of my way!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.360
Eh? They’re still laughing even after the accident.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.740
I guess having an accident can be fun too.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.320
Ah, that was fun.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.260
Really.

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.050
There was some grass stuck on you!

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:53.200
It’s like time has started moving again.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.430
Eh? Started moving?

00:18:56.420 --> 00:19:03.280
I realize the time of our threesomes stopped once you moved to Tokyo…

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:11.290
Now that you’re back, it has started to move again – our time, that is.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:13.660
Is that so?

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:20.030
Every day has been really fun since you came back to this town.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.450
It’s like a continuation of the old days.

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.870
It’s fun for me too.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.380
I’m glad, but…

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:32.270
Now that the time that had stopped has started to move again, where will it take us?

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.830
Nozomu-chan! Kaoruko!

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:48.120
Sumireko!

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:48.120
Sumireko-chan!

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:51.060
Sheesh, where did you guys go?

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:52.900
Oh, we were sliding on the grass.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:55.360
Eh? Sliding on the grass?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.440
It was very nostalgic.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:20:01.590
I can’t believe it. Is this something third-year middle-school students should be doing?

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.410
You too, Sumireko…

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.640
Is climbing on the roof something that third-year middle-school students should do?

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.770
I want to slide on the grass
next time as well.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.400
I want to climb on the roof as well.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.860
Right, Nozomu-chan?

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.360
Yeah.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:25.640
Yeah. For the next vacation day,
let’s go to the beach together.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.180
The beach?

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.680
Yeah! You can see our new swimsuits!

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:30.020
Let’s go together, all three of us!

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.850
Yeah! The three of us, together!

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:33.990
Of course, a threesome!

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:43.250
Today was the first time I saw what Kaoruko- chan and Sumireko-chan were thinking.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.990
If those twins who loved the man had thought it out carefully,

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:52.430
maybe they wouldn’t have needed to turn into little birds in order to live.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.440
The Summer Triangle, huh?

00:20:54.790 --> 00:21:02.240
Note: The Summer Triangle – the 3 stars Deneb, Altair, and Vega

00:20:57.460 --> 00:21:02.240
It’s undoubtedly a summer sky. In Hawaii, it’s about two in the morning.

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.610
Perhaps father can’t sleep and is seeing the same stars.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:10.850
Hey, cut that out!

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.080
Hey, cut that out!

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:18.570
That little…

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.960
Billy! Stop it! Stop!

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:25.030
Onii-chan and Billy seem to be having fun!

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:26.850
They sure get along well.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:27.750
Billy!

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.810
You’ve got to be kidding me!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:58.050
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:58.050
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.060
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.060
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:16.060
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:16.060
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:12.890
This is Momoi Ai.

00:23:12.890 --> 00:23:14.560
This is Mai-sensei!

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:15.870
It’s finally summer vacation!

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:17.770
There’s lots of danger in the sea and in the mountains.

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:19.140
Eh? Where’s the danger?

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:21.000
I can’t say it!

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:22.060
Next time:

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:23.620
The Summer Rocket!
